"""Psychology knowledge cards, knowledge version psychology.v1. Structured, small, sourced.

Rules for editing: a published card is NEVER edited in place. A change = a new card version (same principle_id, version + 1) and the old
version stays in the registry, so an old assessment can always be interpreted (see registry.MANIFEST and the manifest test).
`applicability` holds machine tags `resistance:<value>` (when the engine may use the card) plus optional free-text `context:` notes.
Evidence levels are deliberately conservative; nothing here is a claim about THESE leads (population + limitations say where it was studied).
Sources are citations to be read, not endorsements of effect sizes in this deployment: no conversion figures are derived from them."""
from copilot_psychology.contracts import Domain as D, EvidenceLevel as E, KnowledgeCard, Role as R, SourceType as T, Strategy as S

_GEN = "adult consumers / participants in lab, online or organisational studies; NOT validated for Spanish-speaking Telegram chat leads"


def _c(pid, domain, principle, mechanism, description, applicability, contra, effect, strategies, ev, source, st, limits, population=_GEN,
       role=R.STRATEGY_INPUT, version=1):
    return KnowledgeCard(pid, version, domain, principle, mechanism, description, tuple(applicability), tuple(contra), effect, tuple(strategies), ev,
                         population, source, st, tuple(limits), role)


